The Mercedes-Benz C-Class C230 V6 refers to the W204 generation, specifically models produced from 2007 to 2009 before the facelift (Source [4, 8, 10, 12, 13]). It was powered by a 2.5L V6 engine. This evaluation is based on the W204 C230 V6 relative to the current automotive market.

*   **price\_usd**: As a used car from 2007-2009, the price is significantly lower than a new car today. Used prices vary greatly based on condition, mileage, and location, but are well below the $35,000 average for a new car (Source [21, 27, 36]). Score: 0.80.
*   **total\_cost\_estimate\_5yr\_usd**: While the purchase price is low, an older luxury car will have higher maintenance and potential repair costs than a new economy car (Source [16, 36]). Score: -0.20.
*   **insurance\_usd\_yr**: Insurance groups for the W204 C-Class C230 were moderate for its time, typically in the mid-range (Group 31-32A in the UK) (Source [22, 30, 39]). Relative to modern cars, this is likely around average or slightly below. Score: 0.00.
*   **maint\_usd\_yr**: Maintenance costs for a Mercedes-Benz are generally higher than average (Source [16, 18, 36, 40]). Older cars often require more frequent or extensive maintenance. RepairPal estimates an annual maintenance cost of $727 for a C230 (Source [18]). Score: -0.50.
*   **repair\_risk\_score**: The W204 generation is generally considered reliable for a Mercedes of its era (Source [11, 20, 35]). However, the M272 V6 engine in the C230 had known issues with balance shaft gear wear on earlier models (though less common on later W204s), timing chain tensioners, and potential oil leaks (Source [11, 15, 18, 35]). Other potential issues include steering lock failure and suspension wear (Source [11, 15, 35]). Risk is higher than a top-tier reliable brand but better than some other luxury makes. CarEdge rates the C-Class as worse than average for major repair probability over 10 years (Source [33]). Score: -0.40.
*   **hp**: The C230 V6 had 201-204 hp (Source [1, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 13, 14, 17, 19, 23]). This is around the 200 hp average. Score: 0.00.
*   **torque**: The C230 V6 had 245 Nm (181 lb-ft) (Source [1, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 13, 14, 17, 19]). This is around the 190 lb-ft average. Score: 0.00.
*   **cylinder\_count**: V6 (6 cylinders) (Source [1, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 13, 14, 17, 19, 21, 23]). Above the common 4 cylinders, but common for this class/era. Score: 0.00.
*   **engine\_displacement**: 2.5L (2496 cc) (Source [1, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 13, 14, 17, 19, 21, 23]). Around the average for a V6. Score: 0.00.
*   **accel\_0\_60\_sec**: Around 7.3-8.4 seconds (Source [3, 4, 7, 14, 17, 19, 22, 26]). Real-world tests might be slower (Source [2, 26]). This is around or slightly slower than the 7.5s average. Score: -0.10.
*   **top\_speed**: Around 149 mph (230-240 km/h) (Source [3, 4, 7, 14, 17, 19, 21]). Around the 150 mph average. Score: 0.00.
